-- title:
--   The OSR algebra generated by the system operators $S_\alpha$ and the identity
-- statement:
--   Let $H=\sum_{\alpha}S_\alpha\otimes B_\alpha$ be an expansion of a system–environment Hamiltonian into system operators $S_\alpha$ and environment operators $B_\alpha$ (eq. (5.1)). The **OSR algebra** $\mathcal A$ is the complex associative algebra generated by the $S_\alpha$ and the identity $I$: the set of all operators obtained from $I$ and the $S_\alpha$ by complex linear combinations and operator products,
--   $$
--   \mathcal A=\operatorname{span}_{\mathbb C}\{\,I,\ S_{\alpha_1}S_{\alpha_2}\cdots S_{\alpha_n}\ :\ n\ge 1\,\}.
--   $$
--
--   By Lemma 5.2.1 every OSR operator of the evolution lies in $\mathcal A$, so the algebraic structure of $\mathcal A$ governs which system states can be protected from the environment.
--
--   **Formalization Note** $\mathcal A$ is Mathlib's subalgebra `Algebra.adjoin ℂ (Set.range Sα)` of the matrix algebra; a subalgebra always contains the identity, which is the thesis's "plus the identity". The algebra depends only on the $S_\alpha$; Definition 5.2.2's requirement that the $B_\alpha$ be linearly independent is a condition on the expansion, assumed by the statements that need it.
-- source:
--   Bacon, Decoherence, Control, and Symmetry in Quantum Computers, arXiv:quant-ph/0305025v1, Definition 5.2.1, p.69 (PDF p.86); Definition 5.2.2, p.71 (PDF p.88)

import Mathlib

namespace BaconThesis.DFS

/-- **The OSR algebra.**
Bacon, *Decoherence, Control, and Symmetry in Quantum Computers*, arXiv:quant-ph/0305025v1,
Definition 5.2.1 (complex associative algebra), p.69 (PDF p.86), and Definition 5.2.2
(OSR algebra), p.71 (PDF p.88): the complex associative algebra generated by the system operators
`S_α` of an expansion `H = ∑_α S_α ⊗ B_α` (with linearly independent `B_α`) and the identity `I`,
i.e. all operators obtained from the `S_α` and `I` by complex linear combinations and products.

`osrAlgebra Sα` is the `ℂ`-subalgebra of `Matrix s s ℂ` generated by the family `Sα`.

**Formalization Note.** A Mathlib `Subalgebra` always contains the identity, which is the book's
"plus the identity". The algebra depends only on the system operators `S_α`; the linear
independence of the `B_α` in Definition 5.2.2 is a condition on the expansion and is assumed in
the statements that use it. -/
def osrAlgebra {s ι : Type} [Fintype s] [DecidableEq s] (Sα : ι → Matrix s s ℂ) :
    Subalgebra ℂ (Matrix s s ℂ) :=
  Algebra.adjoin ℂ (Set.range Sα)

end BaconThesis.DFS


